    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T19:04:25Z",
    "body": "Stopped under the requested two-failed-gates rule. I am releasing the claim.\n\nThe four MCP post-options pins pass on the final implementation. They cover explicit document and setup targets, setup isolation, undo/redo, follow-document reset, partial patches, and named input refusals. Restoring upstream tool registration makes the pins fail. Ten guard mutations each fail, and each restored implementation passes. No NC or CL goldens changed.\n\nBoth quick gates against upstream/main fail these tests:\n- stock_source_cross_drill::a_stock_source_cross_drill_at_the_modelled_holes_size_is_excused_its_faceted_wall\n- stock_source_holes::a_hole_kind_in_the_parts_own_hole_or_in_stock_only_material_posts\n\nBoth also fail when rerun individually. The first reports that posed moves are not modelled by the column engine. The second reports that the stock carries a rotation. Both refuse posting because stock simulation did not judge the program. I did not change stock simulation. Clippy was not run after the second failed gate.\n\nThe uncommitted implementation and pins remain in /home/mikekinney/CamcraftCodex/.claude/worktrees/issue-1534 on issue/1534-post-options, based on upstream/main 4f4edcf3. Nothing was pushed and no PR was opened. Red pin output: /tmp/1534-red.txt. Gate logs: gate-logs/quick-20261114-185601/01-app_suites.log and gate-logs/quick-20261114-190035/01-app_suites.log inside that worktree. The issue is free again.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
